  "interpretation": [
    "Streaming hashes moved outside SQL owner locks. Final identity/path stat/open checks still occur under commit locks.",
    "Same-owner wait is measured at storage verification entry through contender COMMIT. Earlier incorrectly timed/overlapping exploratory runs are excluded.",
    "Total publication latency can increase from extra validation/transactions; this is a contention/correctness tradeoff, not a blanket throughput improvement.",
    "Expected publication/revocation 409 conflicts are reported separately from errors. HTTP operations had zero observed errors; no capacity/real-user inference.",
    "Worker number measures one actual complete processing job at concurrency 1, not a sustained distributed-worker throughput result.",
    "Catalog has only seven fixture stories; playlist create/history remove-reset are genuine writes, with preserved CSRF and progress revision semantics. Large populated catalog and long-duration soak remain unverified.",
    "Concurrent winner differs by implementation: hardened publish may legitimately lose to revocation while hashing. Per-action distributions include separately counted expected conflicts; they are not success-only publish latency comparisons.",
    "Publication latency is measured at the service/DB layer; full HTTP authorization/session round trips are not included. The later final-session validation is tested separately."
  ],
  "rateSemantics": "HTTP throughput uses completed requests over actual batch wall time. Publication inverse-mean-latency rates below are NOT observed mixed/concurrent system throughput; use latency/conflict counts for comparisons."
}
